<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Bofors sells missile sights to Austria.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Bofors sells missile sights to Austria.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defence group Bofors AB, a unit of Celsius AB, said on Monday it had sold missile night sights worth 200 million crowns to the Austrian army.</p>
<p>Bofors said in a statement that the sights were linked to missile system BILL that was first introduced into the Austrian defence force in 1989.</p>
<p>The development of the sights for BILL were done by Bofors in cooperation with CelsiusTech Electronics AB.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
